* @title Reset all variables with CLEAR
* @expect >>>
* BEFORE: hello world
* AFTER:  [][]
* <<<
* CLEAR() sets every natural variable back to the null string in one call,
* without disturbing function or keyword definitions. After CLEAR the once-set
* X and Y read as empty.
        X = 'hello'
        Y = 'world'
        OUTPUT = 'BEFORE: ' X ' ' Y
        CLEAR()
        OUTPUT = 'AFTER:  [' X '][' Y ']'
END
